      en: "Koulikoro is a historic river port and administrative capital located on the Niger River, about 60 kilometers downstream from Bamako. As the terminus of the Dakar-Niger Railway, the city served as a vital transshipment point for goods moving between the Atlantic coast and the interior of West Africa. Today, it remains an important industrial center, hosting one of Mali's largest cottonseed oil refineries (HUICOMA) and a major shipyard. Koulikoro is also famous for the 'Nianan Koulou' (Nianan Hill), a sacred site in Manding mythology. Its beautiful riverfront and strategic importance make it a key city in Mali's transport network. Geography K7 — River transport and industrial heritage."
